[block
  'ORD-0005-edit'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-003'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-003/EMS-003.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the signed model'
    '.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-2D-VIEW.md, section 6'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'editing by the links: each operation on the plane is one edit of the tree, the way back writes the source, and the engine reads it again before the picture changes'
  [/tgt]
  [ins
    'build the operations of the signed table, each as one edit of the tree: connect two nodes by a connector of a chosen type, change the type of a connector, move the end of a connector to another node, cut a connector, place a command from the palette of icons, remove a node, change the order of siblings, write the operand of a node, and wrap nodes in a section, a block or a part'
  [/ins]
  [ins
    'offer on each connector the types the two ends admit, and name the operator each one writes: nest, chain, item, sequence, reference and result'
  [/ins]
  [req
    'an edit the tree cannot hold is refused by name before it is applied, and the plane and the source stay as they were'
  [/req]
  [req
    'every edit is undone and redone, and the source after undo is the bytes it was'
  [/req]
  [req
    'what an edit raises is shown where it lands: a new fix, ask or note appears on its node as soon as the engine has read the source again'
  [/req]
  [cnst
    'the plane never writes source by itself: it edits the tree, the way back writes, and the parse of what was written is what the plane shows next'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'nothing vanishes in silence: a node cut from its only connector stays in the package as a root command, and removing a node that holds others asks first what happens to them'
  [/cnst]
  [nev
    'an edit that changes the meaning of a command the user did not touch'
  [/nev]
  [cmp
    'the operations'
    'each operation of the signed table has a case: the source it writes is the source a hand would write for that tree, the engine reads it with no new fix, and the tree read back is the edited tree'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
  [cmp
    'the refusals'
    'each edit the table refuses is refused by its name and leaves the bytes of the source untouched, each seen failing before it counts'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
  [cmp
    'the round trip'
    'over the declared sources, every connector cut and connected again by the same type gives the source back byte for byte'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
[/block]